        "stale aliases are detected through cplus_alloc_is_live / cplus_alloc_check_generation after free; release is refused without calling host free"
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "double/invalid-free detection is heuristic: a bounded 1024-entry recent-free table cannot distinguish every recycled address, so classification is best-effort",
        "freeing a cplus_malloc pointer with host free() bypasses the metadata table, after which cplus_alloc_is_live can report a false live result",
        "cross-allocator free (host allocation passed to cplus_free, or cplus_malloc pointer passed to host free) is undefined behavior; it is refused with EINVAL only when the metadata check detects it"
